    <info>
        <language>en-US</language>
        <category>Met</category>
        <event>Severe Thunderstorm Warning</event>
        <responseType>Shelter</responseType>
        <urgency>Immediate</urgency>
        <severity>Severe</severity>
        <certainty>Observed</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>SVS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>SVW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-07-29T17:49:00-06:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-07-29T17:49:00-06:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-07-29T18:00:00-06:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Billings MT</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued July 29 at 5:49PM MDT until July 29 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Billings MT</headline>
        <description>At 549 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 16 miles east of
Volborg, or 34 miles north of Broadus, moving southeast at 30 mph.

HAZARD...Golf ball size hail and 60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Public reported. At 548 PM, golf ball size hail was
reported 18 miles SSW of Mizpah.

IMPACT...People and animals outdoors will be injured. Expect hail
damage to roofs, siding, windows, and vehicles. Expect
wind damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

Locations impacted include...
Mainly rural areas of Southeastern Custer County.
</description>
        <instruction>Anyone outdoors should move to shelter inside a well-built structure
and stay away from windows. This storm has produced dangerous hail
and is capable of producing damaging winds.

Torrential rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead
to flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
