        <senderName>NWS Riverton WY</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued July 29 at 6:13PM MDT until July 29 at 7:00PM MDT by NWS Riverton WY</headline>
        <description>At 613 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located over Bar Nunn,
which is 7 miles northwest of Casper, moving east at 20 mph.

HAZARD...60 to 65 mph wind gusts and half dollar sized hail.

SOURCE...A peak wind gust of 63 mph was recorded at the Casper-
Natrona County International Airport at 604 PM.

IMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage to
roofs, siding, and trees.

This severe storm will be near...
Northeastern Casper, Bar Nunn, and Homa Hills around 615 PM MDT.

Other locations in the path of this severe thunderstorm include
Evansville.

This includes Interstate 25 between mile markers 176 and 207.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
