    <info>
        <language>en-US</language>
        <category>Met</category>
        <event>Severe Thunderstorm Warning</event>
        <responseType>Shelter</responseType>
        <urgency>Immediate</urgency>
        <severity>Severe</severity>
        <certainty>Observed</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>SVS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>SVW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-07-29T20:17:00-04:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-07-29T20:17:00-04:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-07-29T20:30:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Melbourne FL</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued July 29 at 8:17PM EDT until July 29 at 8:30PM EDT by NWS Melbourne FL</headline>
        <description>At 817 PM EDT, a severe thunderstorm was located over Leesburg,
moving north at 5 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

Locations impacted include...
Leesburg, Lake Griffin, Lake Harris, Fruitland Park, and Leesburg
Airport.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.

Torrential rainfall is occurring with this storm, and may lead to
flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
