        <expires>2025-07-29T18:49:00-07:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS National Tsunami Warning Center</senderName>
        <headline>Tsunami Warning issued July 29 at 5:19PM PDT by NWS National Tsunami Warning Center</headline>
        <description>If you are located in this coastal area, move inland
to higher ground.

Tsunami warnings mean that a tsunami with significant
inundation is possible or is already occurring.  Tsunamis are
a series of waves dangerous many hours after initial arrival
time.  The first wave may not be the largest.

At 425 PM Pacific Daylight Time on July 29 an earthquake with
preliminary magnitude 8.7 occurred 80 miles southeast of
Petropavlovsk Kamchatka.

Estimated tsunami start times for selected sites are;

Shemya             Alaska              440 PM. AKDT. July 29.
Adak               Alaska              540 PM. AKDT. July 29.
Saint Paul         Alaska              655 PM. AKDT. July 29.

The tsunami warning will remain in effect until further notice.
Refer to the internet site tsunami.gov for more information.
</description>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>TSUWCA</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>WMOidentifier</valueName>
            <value>WEPA41 PAAQ 300019</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>NWSheadline</valueName>
            <value>A TSUNAMI WARNING IS NOW IN EFFECT WHICH INCLUDES THE COASTAL AREAS OF ALASKA FROM SAMALGA PASS ALASKA, WHICH IS LOCATED 30 MILES SW OF NIKOLSKI TO ATTU ALASKA</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
