        <senderName>NWS Riverton WY</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued July 29 at 6:21PM MDT until July 29 at 6:45PM MDT by NWS Riverton WY</headline>
        <description>At 621 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 12 miles northwest
of Fort Reno Historical Site, which is 20 miles northeast of Kaycee,
moving southeast at 25 mph.

HAZARD...Quarter size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Damage to vehicles is expected.

This severe thunderstorm will remain over mainly rural areas of east
central Johnson County.

This includes Interstate 25 near mile marker 274.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.

Torrential rainfall is occurring with this storm, and may lead to
flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways.</instruction>
