    <info>
        <language>en-US</language>
        <category>Met</category>
        <event>Special Marine Warning</event>
        <responseType>Avoid</responseType>
        <urgency>Immediate</urgency>
        <severity>Severe</severity>
        <certainty>Likely</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>NWS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>MAW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-07-29T19:24:00-05:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-07-29T19:24:00-05:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-07-29T20:00:00-05:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS New Orleans LA</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued July 29 at 7:24PM CDT until July 29 at 8:00PM CDT by NWS New Orleans LA</headline>
        <description>For the following areas...
Coastal Waters from Port Fourchon LA to Lower Atchafalaya River LA
out 20 nm...

At 723 PM CDT, a cluster of severe thunderstorms were located along a
line extending from near Isle Derniers to Timbalier Island, moving
east at 20 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts to 40 knots and small hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Small craft could be damaged in briefly higher winds and
suddenly higher waves.

Locations impacted include...
Isle Derniers and Timbalier Island.
</description>
        <instruction>Strong winds will be dangerous for boaters or anyone near the water.
Make sure all on board are wearing life jackets. Seek shelter or move
to safe harbor until hazardous weather passes.

Frequent lightning is occurring with these storms. If caught on the
open water stay below deck if possible, keep away from ungrounded
metal objects.

Report severe weather to the Coast Guard or the National Weather
Service.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>MWSLIX</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>WMOidentifier</valueName>
            <value>FZUS74 KLIX 300024</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>NWSheadline</valueName>
            <value>A SPECIAL MARINE WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 800 PM CDT</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>eventMotionDescription</valueName>
            <value>2025-07-30T00:23:00-00:00...storm...270DEG...18KT...29.05,-90.69 29.04,-90.46</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>BLOCKCHANNEL</valueName>
            <value>EAS</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>BLOCKCHANNEL</valueName>
            <value>NWEM</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>VTEC</valueName>
            <value>/O.CON.KLIX.MA.W.0252.000000T0000Z-250730T0100Z/</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>eventEndingTime</valueName>
            <value>2025-07-29T20:00:00-05:00</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>BLOCKCHANNEL</valueName>
            <value>CMAS</value>
        </parameter>
        <area>
            <areaDesc>Coastal Waters from Port Fourchon LA to Lower Atchafalaya River LA out 20 nm</areaDesc>
            <polygon>29.15,-90.8 29.18,-90.68 29.09,-90.35 28.71,-90.35 28.71,-90.42 28.73,-90.58 28.71,-90.68 28.75,-91.02 29.15,-90.8</polygon>
            <geocode>
                <valueName>SAME</valueName>
                <value>077550</value>
            </geocode>
            <geocode>
                <valueName>UGC</valueName>
                <value>GMZ550</value>
            </geocode>
        </area>
    </info>
</alert>




