        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued July 29 at 7:40PM CDT until July 29 at 8:00PM CDT by NWS Sioux Falls SD</headline>
        <description>At 740 PM CDT, severe thunderstorms were located along a line
extending from near Clayton to near Niobrara, moving east at 30 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.

SOURCE...The RWIS near Tripp reported a 68 mph wind gust at
approximately 7:20 pm CDT.

IMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

Locations impacted include...
Springfield, Scotland and Clayton.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.</instruction>
