            <value>MAW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-07-30T19:34:00-04:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-07-30T19:34:00-04:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-07-30T20:30:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Cleveland OH</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued July 30 at 7:34PM EDT until July 30 at 8:30PM EDT by NWS Cleveland OH</headline>
        <description>SMWCLE

The National Weather Service in Cleveland has issued a

* Special Marine Warning for...
Nearshore waters from Reno Beach OH to Vermilion OH...
Open waters from The Islands OH to Vermilion OH...

* Until 830 PM EDT.

* At 734 PM EDT, a severe thunderstorm capable of producing
waterspouts was located near Sandusky Bay, moving southeast at 15
knots.

HAZARD...Waterspouts, wind gusts 34 knots or greater, and small
hail.

SOURCE...Radar.

IMPACT...Waterspouts can easily overturn boats and create locally
hazardous seas. Small craft could be damaged in briefly
higher winds and suddenly higher waves.

* Locations impacted include...
Put-In-Bay, Sandusky Bay, and Kelleys Island.
</description>
        <instruction>Report severe weather to the Coast Guard or the National Weather
Service.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>SMWCLE</value>
        </parameter>
