    <info>
        <language>en-US</language>
        <category>Met</category>
        <event>Flood Advisory</event>
        <responseType>Avoid</responseType>
        <urgency>Expected</urgency>
        <severity>Minor</severity>
        <certainty>Likely</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>NWS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>FAY</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-07-30T19:54:00-04:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-07-30T19:54:00-04:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-07-30T22:00:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Northern Indiana</senderName>
        <headline>Flood Advisory issued July 30 at 7:54PM EDT until July 30 at 10:00PM EDT by NWS Northern Indiana</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.

* WHERE...Portions of northern Indiana, including the following
counties, Allen IN and De Kalb and northwest Ohio, including the
following counties, Defiance and Paulding.

* WHEN...Until 1000 PM EDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.
Overflowing poor drainage areas. Ponding of water in urban or
other areas is occurring or is imminent.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 753 PM EDT, A trained spotter in Hicksville, OH reported
flooded roads in town as of 750 PM EDT. Minor flooding is
ongoing or expected to begin shortly. Between 1.5 and 3
inches of rain have fallen.
- Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are expected
over the area. This additional rain will result in minor
flooding.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Fort Wayne, Hicksville, Antwerp, Woodburn, Grabill, St. Joe,
Leo-cedarville, Concord, Harlan, Cuba, Spencerville In Dekalb
County and Saint Joe.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
