        <headline>Flood Advisory issued July 30 at 7:58PM EDT until July 30 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Detroit/Pontiac MI</headline>
        <description>The Flood Advisory will expire at 8 PM EDT this evening for a
portion of southeast Michigan, including the following area, Wayne.
The heavy rain has ended. Urban and small stream flooding is no
longer expected to pose a threat. Please continue to heed remaining
road closures.

Additional periods of rainfall will still be possible this evening,
but the main flood threat has ended.
</description>
