        <expires>2025-07-30T20:30:00-04:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Cleveland OH</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued July 30 at 8:14PM EDT until July 30 at 8:30PM EDT by NWS Cleveland OH</headline>
        <description>For the following areas...
Nearshore waters from Reno Beach OH to Vermilion OH...
Open waters from The Islands OH to Vermilion OH...

At 814 PM EDT, a severe thunderstorm capable of producing waterspouts
was located near Sandusky Bay, moving southeast at 15 knots.

HAZARD...Waterspouts, wind gusts to 40 knots, and small hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Waterspouts can easily overturn boats and create locally
hazardous seas. Small craft could be damaged in briefly
higher winds and suddenly higher waves.

Locations impacted include...
Sandusky Bay and Kelleys Island.
</description>
        <instruction>Report severe weather to the Coast Guard or the National Weather
Service.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>MWSCLE</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>WMOidentifier</valueName>
            <value>FZUS71 KCLE 310014</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>NWSheadline</valueName>
            <value>A SPECIAL MARINE WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 830 PM EDT</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
