        <senderName>NWS Lake Charles LA</senderName>
        <headline>Special Marine Warning issued July 30 at 7:35PM CDT until July 30 at 8:15PM CDT by NWS Lake Charles LA</headline>
        <description>SMWLCH

The National Weather Service in Lake Charles has issued a

* Special Marine Warning for...
Waters from Cameron LA to High Island TX from 20 to 60 NM...
Waters from Intracoastal City to Cameron LA from 20 to 60 NM...

* Until 815 PM CDT.

* At 735 PM CDT, a strong thunderstorm was located over West Cameron
198, or 32 nm south of Cameron, moving south at 20 knots.

HAZARD...Wind gusts to nearly 50 knots.

SOURCE...Radar.

IMPACT...Small craft could be damaged in briefly higher winds and
suddenly higher waves.

* Locations impacted include...
West Cameron 178, West Cameron 198, West Cameron 196, West Cameron
173, West Cameron 192, West Cameron 170, West Cameron 171, West
Cameron 180, West Cameron 215, West Cameron 248, and West Cameron
205.
</description>
        <instruction>Move to safe harbor until hazardous weather passes.

Frequent lightning is occurring with this storm. If caught on the
open water stay below deck if possible, keep away from ungrounded
metal objects.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
