        <headline>Flood Advisory issued July 30 at 8:38PM EDT until July 30 at 8:45PM EDT by NWS Detroit/Pontiac MI</headline>
        <description>The Flood Advisory will expire at 845 PM EDT this evening for a
portion of southeast Michigan, including the following areas,
Washtenaw and Wayne. A Flash Flood Warning remains in effect for a
portion of the advisory area.

Flooding is no longer expected to pose a threat, outside of the
Flash Flood Warning area of the advisory. Please continue to heed
remaining road closures.
</description>
