    <info>
        <language>en-US</language>
        <category>Met</category>
        <event>Severe Thunderstorm Warning</event>
        <responseType>Shelter</responseType>
        <urgency>Immediate</urgency>
        <severity>Severe</severity>
        <certainty>Observed</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>SVS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>SVW</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-07-30T19:45:00-05:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-07-30T19:45:00-05:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-07-30T20:00:00-05:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Springfield MO</senderName>
        <headline>Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued July 30 at 7:45PM CDT until July 30 at 8:00PM CDT by NWS Springfield MO</headline>
        <description>At 745 PM CDT, a severe thunderstorm was located over Aurora, moving
east at 10 mph.

HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and penny size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.

Locations impacted include...
Monett, Aurora, Marionville, Verona, Pleasant Ridge, and Madry.
</description>
        <instruction>For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a
building.

Torrential rainfall is occurring with this storm, and may lead to
flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>SVSSGF</value>
        </parameter>
